IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-1`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 8 (2 of 3): regulations 29 to 33 (National Insurance credits, Chapter 3,
-- first part: credits under the 1975 Regulations, working tax credit, universal credit,
-- men approaching pensionable age, spouses and civil partners of members of the forces).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
-- Same inputs-not-in-the-text as spr-part8-credits-1.l4: the lower earnings limit, the
-- qualifying earnings factor, the 1975 Regulations, the 1992 Act and the Contributions
-- Regulations 2001 are not inputs, so the facts they decide are plain inputs.
-- In the source text, regulation 30(1)(b) and regulation 32(4)(a) carry a literal
-- "..." where words appear to have been removed (lines 369 and 392 of the text file);
-- they are quoted as they stand and encoded on the words that remain (fork F30).

§ `Part 8: National Insurance Credits (continued)`

§§ `Chapter 3: Crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year (regulations 29 to 39)`

§§§ `Regulation 29: credits under the 1975 Regulations`

DECLARE ProvisionOfThe1975Regulations IS ONE OF
    `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)`
    `regulation 7A (credits for carer's allowance or carer support payment)`
    `regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit)`
    `regulation 8A (credits for unemployment)`
    `regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work)`
    `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)`
    `regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.)`
    `regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody)`
    `regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces)`
    `another provision of the 1975 Regulations`

-- Gloss: the nine provisions of the 1975 Regulations that regulation 29(2) lists
-- carry over: a person credited under one of them is also credited, with the same
-- earnings or contributions, for Part 1 of the 2014 Act.
-- src:356 | (2) The provisions specified are—
-- src:357 | (a) regulation 7 (credits for approved training);
-- src:358 | (b) regulation 7A (credits for carer’s allowance or carer support payment);
-- src:359 | (c) regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit);
-- src:360 | (d) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment);
-- src:361 | (e) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work);
-- src:362 | (f) regulation 9B (credits for jury service);
-- src:363 | (g) regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.);
-- src:364 | (h) regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody);
-- src:365 | (i) regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty’s forces).
@ref Regulation 29(2) (src:356-365)
GIVEN provision IS A ProvisionOfThe1975Regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `another provision of the 1975 Regulations` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:355 | (1) Where a person is credited with earnings or contributions under the provisions of the 1975 Regulations specified in paragraph (2), the person is also to be credited with those earnings or contributions for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 29(1) (src:355)
GIVEN provision IS A ProvisionOfThe1975Regulations
      `the person is credited with earnings or contributions under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 29(1): the person is also credited for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act` provision `the person is credited with earnings or contributions under that provision` MEANS
        `the person is credited with earnings or contributions under that provision`
    AND `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` provision

§§§ `Regulation 30: credits for persons in receipt of working tax credit`

-- "Working tax credit" is a Tax Credits Act 2002 benefit for people in low-paid work.
DECLARE KindOfEarner IS ONE OF
    `an employed earner`
    `a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, who would otherwise ... be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution`
    `a person excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001`
    `another kind of person`

DECLARE WorkingTaxCreditFacts HAS
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS A KindOfEarner
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS A NUMBER

-- Gloss, paragraph (2): when the credit is paid to a couple, the person paragraph (1)
-- means is the one member assessed as having earnings, if only one is; if both are, the
-- member the credit is paid to.
-- src:372 | (2) Where working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple, the reference in paragraph (1) to the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid is a reference to —
-- src:373 | (a) where only one member of the couple is assessed for the purposes of the award of working tax credit as having income consisting of earnings, that member, or
-- src:374 | (b) where the earnings of each member are assessed, the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid.
@ref Regulation 30(2) (src:372-374)
GIVEN facts IS A WorkingTaxCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 30(2): the person is the person that paragraph (1) refers to` facts MEANS
    IF NOT (facts's `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF facts's `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings`
         THEN facts's `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings`
         ELSE facts's `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid`

-- src:367 | (1) Where working tax credit is paid to a person in respect of a week in which the person is—
-- src:368 | (a) an employed earner,
-- src:369 | (b) a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, who would otherwise... be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution, or
-- src:370 | (c) excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001,
-- src:371 | the person is to be credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of that week.
@ref Regulation 30(1) (src:367-371)
GIVEN facts IS A WorkingTaxCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 30(1): the kind of person is one the paragraph names` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the kind of person the person is in the week`
    WHEN `an employed earner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, who would otherwise ... be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of person` THEN FALSE

-- src:375 | (3) Paragraph (1) does not apply to—
-- src:376 | (a) a person in respect of a week in which the person is entitled to be credited with earnings under—
-- src:377 | (i) regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit),
-- src:378 | (ii) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment), or
-- src:379 | (iii) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work),
-- src:380 | of the 1975 Regulations; or
-- src:381 | (b) a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
@ref Regulation 30(3) (src:375-381)
GIVEN facts IS A WorkingTaxCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 30(3): paragraph (1) does not apply` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations`
    OR facts's `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week`

@ref Regulation 30(1) to (3) (src:367-381)
GIVEN facts IS A WorkingTaxCreditFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` facts MEANS
        facts's `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week`
    AND `regulation 30(2): the person is the person that paragraph (1) refers to` facts
    AND `regulation 30(1): the kind of person is one the paragraph names` facts
    AND NOT (`regulation 30(3): paragraph (1) does not apply` facts)

-- The credit is earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force for the week.
@ref Regulation 30(1) (src:367-371)
GIVEN facts IS A WorkingTaxCreditFacts
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 30(1): the earnings credited` facts MEANS
    IF `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` facts
    THEN JUST (facts's `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§§ `Regulation 31: credits for persons entitled to universal credit`

-- src:384 | A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of a week for any part of which the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act.
@ref Regulation 31 (src:384)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 31: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week` MEANS
    `the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act for any part of the week`

§§§ `Regulation 32: credits for persons approaching pensionable age`

DECLARE ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts HAS
    `the man's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS A DATE
    `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
    `the number of days the man is absent from Great Britain during the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the man is a self-employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS A NUMBER

-- Gloss, paragraph (2): the week falls in the tax year in which the man reaches the age
-- that is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day, or in a later tax year
-- before the one in which he turns 65.
-- src:387 | (2) This paragraph applies to a week which falls within—
-- src:388 | (a) the year in which the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day, and
-- src:389 | (b) a subsequent year prior to that in which he attains the age of 65.
@ref Regulation 32(2) (src:387-389)
GIVEN facts IS A ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 32(2): the week is one to which paragraph (2) applies` facts MEANS
        weekYear EQUALS womanAgeYear
    OR (weekYear GREATER THAN womanAgeYear AND weekYear LESS THAN age65Year)
    WHERE
        weekYear MEANS `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (facts's `the first day of the week`)
        womanAgeYear MEANS `the tax year in which the day falls` (facts's `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day`)
        age65Year MEANS `the tax year in which the day falls` (`add years` (facts's `the man's date of birth`) 65)

-- src:390 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply to a week which falls within a year during which the man is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days.
@ref Regulation 32(3) (src:390)
GIVEN facts IS A ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 32(3): the man was absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days in the year` facts MEANS
    facts's `the number of days the man is absent from Great Britain during the year` GREATER THAN 182

-- src:391 | (4) Paragraph (1) applies to a man who is a self-employed earner only if he—
-- src:392 | (a) ... would be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, or
-- src:393 | (b) is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which this regulation applies.
@ref Regulation 32(4) (src:391-393)
GIVEN facts IS A ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 32(4): paragraph (1) applies to the man` facts MEANS
    IF facts's `the man is a self-employed earner`
    THEN       facts's `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act`
            OR facts's `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies`
    ELSE TRUE

-- src:386 | (1) Subject to paragraph (4), a man born before 6th October 1953 is to be credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of a week to which paragraph (2) applies.
@ref Regulation 32(1) (src:386)
GIVEN facts IS A ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 32(1): the man is credited with earnings for the week` facts MEANS
        facts's `the man's date of birth` LESS THAN YMD 1953 10 6
    AND `regulation 32(2): the week is one to which paragraph (2) applies` facts
    AND NOT (`regulation 32(3): the man was absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days in the year` facts)
    AND `regulation 32(4): paragraph (1) applies to the man` facts

@ref Regulation 32(1) (src:386)
GIVEN facts IS A ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 32(1): the earnings credited` facts MEANS
    IF `regulation 32(1): the man is credited with earnings for the week` facts
    THEN JUST (facts's `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§§ `Regulation 33: credits for spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces (Chapter 3)`

-- Regulation 33 repeats regulation 28 word for word except paragraph (3): checked by diffing
-- lines 336-352 of the source against lines 395-411, which differ at one line only (the
-- years the regulation is for). Paragraphs (1), (2), (4), (5) and (6) are therefore the same
-- rules and are called, not written twice.
-- Gloss, paragraph (3): a week in a tax year beginning on or after 6 April 2016 for which
-- the member's earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
-- src:399 | (3) This regulation applies to a week which falls within a year beginning on or after 6th April 2016 for which the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty’s forces exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
@ref Regulation 33(3) (src:399)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 33(3): the regulation applies to the week` facts MEANS
        `the first day of the tax year` taxYear AT LEAST YMD 2016 4 6
    AND facts's `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` GREATER THAN facts's `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    WHERE
        taxYear MEANS `regulation 25(3): the tax year in which the week falls` (facts's `the first day of the week`)

-- src:395 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person who satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2) for any part of a week to which this regulation applies is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of that week.
@ref Regulation 33(1) (src:395)
GIVEN facts IS A ForcesSpouseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 33(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` facts MEANS
        `regulation 28(2): the conditions are satisfied` facts
    AND `regulation 33(3): the regulation applies to the week` facts
    AND NOT (`regulation 28(4): paragraph (1) does not apply` facts)
    AND `regulation 28(5) and (6): a valid application has been received` facts
